Depends: kernel (=6.12.57~6fb8264c57923364b0c04125e648d82c-r1), kmod-crypto-cbc, kmod-crypto-hmac, kmod-crypto-rng, kmod-crypto-sha256, kmod-keys-trusted
Source: feeds/base/kernel/linux
SourceName: kernel
License: GPL-2.0-only
LicenseFiles: COPYING
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1760997621
CPE-ID: cpe:/o:linux:linux_kernel
Architecture: aarch64_generic
Installed-Size: 40960
Filename: kmod-keys-encrypted_6.12.57-r1_aarch64_generic.ipk
Size: 10170
SHA256sum: 06396305aadc1474a53efa6db3ec25a7d89da941108b17e64f21629c4d53c6bb
Description:  This module provides support for create/encrypting/decrypting keys
 in the kernel.  Encrypted keys are kernel generated random numbers,
 which are encrypted/decrypted with a 'master' symmetric key. The
 'master' key can be either a trusted-key or user-key type.
 Userspace only ever sees/stores encrypted blobs.

Package: kmod-keys-trusted
Version: 6.12.57-r1
Depends: kernel (=6.12.57~6fb8264c57923364b0c04125e648d82c-r1), kmod-crypto-hash, kmod-crypto-hmac, kmod-crypto-sha1, kmod-tpm
Source: feeds/base/kernel/linux
SourceName: kernel
License: GPL-2.0-only
LicenseFiles: COPYING
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1760997621
CPE-ID: cpe:/o:linux:linux_kernel
Architecture: aarch64_generic
Installed-Size: 20480
Filename: kmod-keys-trusted_6.12.57-r1_aarch64_generic.ipk
Size: 4728
SHA256sum: 8f6e599f231642449f023453f700c6e540b6c342de43e6d65f2999e5164a323e
Description:  This module provides support for creating, sealing, and unsealing
 keys in the kernel. Trusted keys are random number symmetric keys,
 generated and RSA-sealed by the TPM. The TPM only unseals the keys,
 if the boot PCRs and other criteria match.  Userspace will only ever
 see encrypted blobs.

